  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is driven by three primary failure modes: premature breakeven stops turning gross winners into net fee-drag losses (Trades 4 and 8), tight stop-loss whipsaws (0.4%\u20130.65%) occurring during the low-liquidity mid-day lull between 10:35 and 13:45, and unmitigated long bias during a broad market sell-off on October 22 (5 losses on the same day, including 3 repeat entries on TATASTEEL). Furthermore, the low 1.3x sweep volume threshold failed to filter out retail noise, resulting in immediate mean-reversion against our entries.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities, a 0.4% stop loss combined with a 1.0R breakeven trigger sits squarely inside the typical 5-minute bid-ask and microstructure noise band during mid-day consolidation, causing trades to get stopped out before institutional trend continuation can materialize while brokerage and statutory fees erode account equity.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.2,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 1.8,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.25,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #45 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nForensic analysis of Cycle #45 revealed severe fee drag (\u20b954.23 fees vs \u20b9-37.50 Net P&L) and a 26.7% win rate caused by mid-day stop hunts and premature breakeven triggers. To eliminate false breakouts and noise-induced whipsaws, `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` has been raised from 1.3x to 1.8x to demand genuine institutional participation at liquidity sweeps. Stop losses (`min_sl_pct`) are widened from 0.40% to 0.55% to survive normal NSE 5-minute intraday retracements, while `min_target_pct` is expanded to 1.20% and `breakeven_trigger_r` pushed to 1.25R to ensure winning excursions easily clear statutory transaction costs and give trades room to breathe before locking in stops."
